<p class="font-secondary"><em>This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article.</em></p>
<section id="_adsm93_" lang="en" class="supplementary-materials"><h3 class="pmc_sec_title">Supplementary Materials</h3>
<section class="sm xbox font-sm" id="db_ds_supplementary-material1_reqid_"><div class="caption p"><span>Supplementary Tables</span></div>
<div class="media p"><div class="caption">
<a href="/articles/instance/7328899/bin/NIHMS1589633-supplement-Supplementary_Tables.xlsx" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" class="usa-link">NIHMS1589633-supplement-Supplementary_Tables.xlsx</a><sup> (18.7MB, xlsx) </sup>
</div></div></section></section><section id="_adda93_" lang="en" class="data-availability-statement"><h3 class="pmc_sec_title">Data Availability Statement</h3>
<p>The PRISM Repurposing dataset, including screening data and all
metadata, is available at the Cancer Dependency Map portal at <a href="https://depmap.org/repurposing" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://depmap.org/repurposing</a>.</p>
<p>Raw and processed PRISM viability data are available from the Cancer
Dependency Map portal (<a href="https://depmap.org/repurposing" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://depmap.org/repurposing</a>) and archived via Figshare
(doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.9393293" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">10.6084/m9.figshare.9393293</a>). An interactive
version of <a href="#F2" class="usa-link">Figure 2a</a> and <a href="#F4" class="usa-link">Figure 4</a> (with accompanying raw data) is also
available on the Cancer Dependency Map portal; scatter plot source data is also
deposited in Figshare (doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.9393293" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">10.6084/m9.figshare.9393293</a>). The cell line features used for
biomarker analysis are listed in <a href="#SD1" class="usa-link">Supplementary Table 10</a> and also
archived via Figshare (doi:<a href="https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.10277810" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">10.6084/m9.figshare.10277810</a>). RNA sequencing data were
deposited in the Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO, accession number <a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE133299" class="usa-link" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GSE133299</a>). All
other data supporting the findings of this study are available from the
corresponding author on reasonable request.</p></section></section></section></section></article>

                      

                    </main>
